# What never needs to reach the Docker daemon.
#
# The build context is the repository root, so this file governs the whole tree.
# Everything here is either rebuilt inside the image anyway, useless to it, or
# something that must not be copied into an image at all.

# Build output. The image compiles from source; a target/ from the host would be
# a different platform's classes at best, and would defeat the layer cache at
# worst.
target/
**/target/
build/
**/build/
*.jar
*.war

# Frontend build artefacts. Both images are built from this context, so this
# applies to the frontend's own build too: node_modules is installed inside the
# image by `npm ci` and dist/ is produced there by `vite build`. Sending the
# host's copies would mean tens of thousands of files over the wire, a cache
# miss on every build, and — worse — a dist/ that might be older than the source
# it was supposed to be built from.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
frontend/dist/

# Version control and tooling.
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
.claude/

# Secrets and local overrides. An .env here would end up in the build context
# and, one careless COPY later, inside the image.
.env
.env.*

# Test and coverage artefacts.
**/surefire-reports/
**/failsafe-reports/
**/jacoco.exec

# Documentation and local noise.
docs/
*.md
*.log
